  "notes": [
    "Planet maps are equirectangular. Solar System Scope adjusts colors and fills unmapped areas with illustrative terrain.",
    "Neptune and Uranus are 2048 x 1024 source maps and are never upscaled.",
    "The Pluto color preview is 2048 x 1024, resized by the NASA image CDN from its 5926 x 2963 original. The original color image is not bundled.",
    "Procedural atmosphere or relief overlays are artistic visual effects and do not represent newly observed detail.",
    "The provider URLs for Jupiter, Saturn and Sun say 8k, but their actual JPEG dimensions are 4096 x 2048. These originals are stored and catalogued as 4K, never upscaled.",
    "The NASA and USGS Pluto maps contain black regions at the southern pole where data are unavailable. Any visual fill in those areas is illustrative, not observed surface data.",
    "Pluto detail comes from the USGS New Horizons LORRI/MVIC global 300 m monochrome mosaic, native 24888 x 12444. Two WMS 4096 x 4096 hemispheres provide 8192 x 4096 equivalent sampling, with no local image edits. Coverage and actual observed detail vary across the globe. The NASA color preview provides tint in the shader.",
    "Earth and Venus use separate native 2048 x 1024 cloud/atmosphere maps from Solar System Scope."
  ],
